	(text_box "PROFET U9 -- PINOUT VERIFIED, Infineon BTS7008-2EPA Rev. 1.21 Table 2 (2024-07-29)\nEP/15 VS (exposed pad, the ONLY supply pin)   1 GND   2 IN0   3 DEN   4 IS   5 DSEL\n6 IN1   7, 11 n.c. (internally not bonded)    8-10 OUT1   12-14 OUT0\nTable 2 note 1: \"All output pins of the channel must be connected together on the PCB.\" All three pins of each channel are therefore\nmodelled and tied on this sheet, and the layout must carry the full channel current on every one of them.\nFOOTPRINT (Task 8): Package_SO:Infineon_PG-TSDSO-14-22, which ships with KiCad.  Its pad 15 is the 2.65 x 4 mm thermal pad, which is\nwhy VS is numbered 15 here.  PG-TSDSO-14-22 is the former name of the same package -- the datasheet's revision history records the\nrename."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 97.1 0)
		(size 103.19 13.84)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "06448ca0-599e-56e8-bd13-7764b2e553c2")
	)
	(text_box "PROFET SENSE CHAIN -- HOW R81 WAS SIZED\nkILIS = 5400 (Table 22, at IL14 = 2.8 A, +/-5.8%; 5450 at 5.5 A).  At the Denali's 3.3 A per\nchannel (spec 2.2) the IS pin therefore sources IL / kILIS = 611 uA.\nR81 = 2.2 kOhm puts that at 1.34 V, comfortably mid-scale for ADC1 at 11 dB attenuation (useful range ~0.15 to 2.45 V on GPIO 34).\nFull scale then corresponds to 6.0 A -- above the 3.3 A working point, below the 7.5 A nominal rating, so a genuine overcurrent still\nreads on scale instead of pinning.  The 0.15 V ADC floor corresponds to 368 mA, so an open channel (IL(OL) is ~21 mA, Table 22) reads\nas a hard zero and is unambiguous.\nR82 (RIS_PROT) and R83 (RADC) are NOT optional.  Under a fault the IS pin saturates: Table 20 gives IIS(SAT) = 4.1 to 15 mA and VSIS_F\n= VS - VIS of only 0.5 V typ / 1 V max, so the sense node sits within a volt of battery -- about 12.5 V.  R83 is what keeps that off\nGPIO 34, with D21 clamping the remainder to +3V3_ALW at under 2 mA.\nC47 (220 pF) with R83 gives the ~1 us time constant the datasheet asks for.  C48 (10 nF) at the ADC end supplies the SAR sample-and-\nhold charge locally, which is what makes a 4.7 kOhm series resistor harmless; tau = 47 us, so firmware must settle >= 250 us after\nselecting a channel with DSEL before reading."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 112.44 0)
		(size 103.19 21.24)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "210396ac-f9ed-5b39-baf3-db3189a79378")
	)
	(text_box "CORNER CONNECTORS CAN BE MIS-MATED -- THIS IS A SAFETY ITEM (spec 9.2)\nAll four are identical Superseal 1.0 4-way parts.  Swapping front for rear reverses the\nindicators, and the firmware cannot detect it.  Each connector carries a distinct keying or\ncolour code in its Value field: FL key A / black, FR key B / grey, RL key C / brown,\nRR key D / natural.  Carry these into the harness build and the install instructions."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 162.9 0)
		(size 103.19 9.4)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "29977fac-d297-5264-8870-4c1d1d0de826")
	)
	(text_box "SENSE-PATH PROTECTION (I15)\nEach sense node reaches its mux input through 10 kOhm (R64-R75) with a clamp to +3V3_SW.\nThe SERIES RESISTOR is what actually bounds a fault: at 24 V on a sense node it admits 2 mA,\nfar inside the ADG706's input rating.  The clamps (D9-D20) are redundancy.\nC44, 10 nF at the mux output, supplies the ADC's sample-and-hold charge locally, which is what makes 10 kOhm series resistors harmless.\ntau = 100 us, so firmware must wait >= 500 us after each mux step before reading.  100 nF would stretch that to 1 ms.\nA quad diode array may replace D9-D20 at layout to save area."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 83.24 0)
		(size 103.19 12.36)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "770dfe59-ff42-5f07-9de4-db69f52ade64")
	)
	(text_box "PTCs (F2-F5), one per string\nIsolates a shorted string so one crushed cable cannot extinguish all four corners (spec 5.2).\nLittelfuse 1206L050/24: Ihold 0.50 A at 23 C, 0.31 A at 65 C, against an 80 mA per-string load.\nThat is a 3.9x margin at the hot internal temperature, which is the case that matters."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 173.8 0)
		(size 103.19 7.92)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "84cfe987-a8ad-5385-bf6a-3eecf63e7e5f")
	)
	(text_box "ACCEPTANCE (spec 5, 9.1, 9.2)\n- PCA9685 on +3V3_SW, I2C, LED0-11 -> the 12 RGB switch inputs IN ChannelIndex ORDER:\n  LED0,1,2 = FL R,G,B;  LED3,4,5 = FR R,G,B;  LED6,7,8 = RL R,G,B;  LED9,10,11 = RR R,G,B.\n  LED12-15 UNUSED.\n- 12x discrete logic-level N-MOSFET, gate direct from PCA9685, sense shunt in each source leg\n- 12 SENSE_* nodes -> 16:1 analog mux (MUX_S0-S3) -> RGB_ISNS -> GPIO 32 (ADC1_CH4)\n- NO SPI anywhere on this board\n- Dual PROFET from VBAT, inputs PWM_DEN_A/B from ESP32 LEDC on GPIO 18/19, NOT the PCA9685\n- PROFET: ONE sense output -> ISNS_DEN (GPIO 34) with scaling resistor; DEN_DSEL selects\n  which channel IS reports\n- 4x PTC, one per string, on the +24V feeds\n- All 14 PWM_* nets have a pulldown to GND\n- 4 corner connectors, keyed/colour-coded differently from each other\n- Denali connector: 2 switched positives + 1 shared ground\n- Output snubber footprints present but DNP"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 13 0)
		(size 103.19 24.2)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8af0977f-9011-5cf2-b316-73541fab9d1f")
	)
	(text_box "SENSE CHAIN (spec 5.1) -- VALUES REVISED, THE PLAN TEXT IS STALE\n10 ohm x 26.7 mA = 267 mV at full channel current (133 mV if the 6 cm strip length is used).\nADC1 at 0 dB attenuation (0-1.1 V range).  Classification is open (~0 mV) / working (~267 mV) /\nshorted (saturated) -- NOT precision current metering.\nTask 6 of the plan still says \"1 ohm\" and \"140 mV\", and asks for 2512 >= 1 W shunts.  Those figures predate the RGB load being\ncorrected downward by about 4x (spec 2.2); part-selection.md rows 1b.1-1b.3 carry the current values and explicitly WITHDRAW the 2512\nrequirement.\nSampling is on-demand: firmware drives one channel to 100%, steps the mux, reads, advances. The same sweep serves as the installation\nself-test."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 38.7 0)
		(size 103.19 15.32)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9d60a132-6c5f-5fd8-80ff-8d1416124c4d")
	)
	(text_box "SHUNT RATING DEPENDS ON A FIRMWARE BEHAVIOUR -- READ THIS BEFORE CHANGING EITHER\nNormal dissipation in a 10 ohm shunt is 26.7 mA^2 x 10 = 7 mW, so an 0805 or 1206 is ample.\nA SHORTED channel is different.  The boost then current-limits at roughly 0.5 A, which puts about 2.5 W into that one shunt -- ten\ntimes a 1206's rating.  It survives only because the diagnostic sweep is brief and because firmware LATCHES A SHORTED CHANNEL OFF once\nit classifies one.  That makes the shunt package rating conditional on firmware behaviour, which is exactly the kind of cross-domain\ndependency that gets lost between disciplines.\nIt is written down in three places on purpose: here, in part-selection.md, and it belongs in the firmware spec (spec section 12) when\nthat is written.  If firmware does NOT latch off, move the shunts to 2512 1 W."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 55.52 0)
		(size 103.19 13.84)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a3ef6642-894e-58c9-9219-5a6dc6de0be7")
	)
	(text_box "WHY ~OE IS PULLED LOW (R78) RATHER THAN HIGH\nThe plan says \"OE tied so outputs are disabled by default\".  Taken literally that means pulling\n~OE HIGH -- but no GPIO is allocated to release it, so the board would be permanently dark.\n\"Disabled by default\" is already delivered twice over without this pin: the PCA9685 sits on +3V3_SW so it is unpowered in sleep, and it\npowers up with MODE1 SLEEP set and every LEDn register cleared, i.e. outputs off.  R78 holds ~OE low so the part is usable; the safe\nstate comes from the rail and the power-on register defaults."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 70.86 0)
		(size 103.19 10.88)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b62af860-9e32-5b90-9a35-d17830e2df9e")
	)
	(text_box "PROFET CONTROL LINES -- WHY THE PULLDOWNS ARE ON THE MCU SIDE\nR79/R80/R84/R85 are the datasheet's RIN, RDEN and RDSEL (Table 24, 4.7 kOhm): they protect the\nMCU during overvoltage and reverse polarity, and they are what allows the outputs to switch\nOFF if the module loses its ground.\nAll four inputs must be held low while the ESP32 is in reset or deep sleep -- that is also what keeps the PROFET in Sleep mode (0.6 uA)\nrather than Stand-by, which needs INn, DEN and DSEL all low, and GPIO 18/19 float in reset.  R86/R87 do that for the two PWM lines;\nEN_DIAG and DEN_DSEL already have R35 and R34 in mcu_can's passive-defaults block, so they are not duplicated here.\nThey are deliberately on the MCU side of the series resistors.  In series the two would form a divider: 3.3 V x 10 / 14.7 = 2.24 V at\nthe pin, against a guaranteed-high threshold of 2.0 V max (Table 7).  A 240 mV margin over temperature and tolerance is not a margin.\nOn the MCU side the pin is driven through 4.7 kOhm into a microamp input, so the drop is negligible."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 135.18 0)
		(size 103.19 16.8)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c29b7404-01cc-546d-8523-9abb5e1aafc7")
	)
	(text_box "PROFET -- WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT FITTED\nNo RPD (47 kOhm output pulldown), ROL or T1.  Those exist only for OFF-state open-load\ndiagnosis, which spec 5.3 does not ask for; ON-state sense through IS covers what this design\nneeds.  RPD would also draw ~290 uA per channel whenever the output is on."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 153.48 0)
		(size 103.19 7.92)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f046ddfe-e344-59f1-be5b-4562b2efa7e1")
	)
